WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.167 --> 00:00:01.325
- Are you okay?

00:00:01.325 --> 00:00:03.402
Oh my God, please don't bite me.

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:04.632
I'm so sorry.

00:00:04.632 --> 00:00:07.261
(polka music)

00:00:07.261 --> 00:00:09.527
- I just hope the dog likes the bath

00:00:09.527 --> 00:00:11.267
because I don't want it
to be scared. (laughing)

00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:12.883
- I have given a cat a bath before,

00:00:12.883 --> 00:00:14.599
and it was an awful experience.

00:00:14.599 --> 00:00:16.182
So, I'm kind of just hoping this

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.540
is a little bit better than that.

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:19.023
- [Interviewer] Does anyone
have any last thoughts

00:00:19.023 --> 00:00:20.418
before you meet the dog?

00:00:20.418 --> 00:00:22.109
- It's three of us against one,

00:00:22.109 --> 00:00:23.368
so I think we can do this. (laughing)

00:00:23.368 --> 00:00:24.225
- We'll be fine.

00:00:24.225 --> 00:00:25.058
- Yeah.

00:00:26.866 --> 00:00:30.366
(intense acoustics)

00:00:32.896 --> 00:00:34.221
- Oh, hi.

00:00:34.221 --> 00:00:35.597
Hi.

00:00:35.597 --> 00:00:36.984
- He's really nice.

00:00:36.984 --> 00:00:39.211
I'm just like not really
sure how to handle dogs.

00:00:39.211 --> 00:00:41.364
- I guess we're gonna
give a dog a bath now.

00:00:41.364 --> 00:00:42.383
- Aw, he looks so scared.

00:00:42.383 --> 00:00:43.716
- Aww.
- I know.

00:00:44.882 --> 00:00:45.922
- It kind of looks like
he's taking a shower

00:00:45.922 --> 00:00:47.839
- Yeah, look at him go.

00:00:49.436 --> 00:00:51.554
- Are you into this?

00:00:51.554 --> 00:00:53.038
He's so slippery.

00:00:53.038 --> 00:00:56.687
- Alright. Let's get that little poof.

00:00:56.687 --> 00:00:58.211
(water splashing)

00:00:58.211 --> 00:00:59.667
- He's kind of a rat.

00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:01.119
- Oh, perfect.

00:01:01.119 --> 00:01:03.248
Yeah, if you could just
face that way. (chuckling)

00:01:03.248 --> 00:01:04.698
Wow.

00:01:04.698 --> 00:01:07.281
(soft jingles)

00:01:08.278 --> 00:01:09.397
- I'm soaking.

00:01:09.397 --> 00:01:10.613
- Oh, no.

00:01:10.613 --> 00:01:11.446
Slippery.

00:01:11.446 --> 00:01:14.111
- [Interviewer] Okay, Danielle,
can you put him back in?

00:01:14.111 --> 00:01:15.047
(water pouring)

00:01:15.047 --> 00:01:16.022
- You're, so clean

00:01:16.022 --> 00:01:18.833
(dog shaking water)
(group sighs)

00:01:18.833 --> 00:01:21.013
- Just when we started to like you.

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:22.902
Alright, here we go.

00:01:22.902 --> 00:01:23.851
Okay, maybe my lap's

00:01:23.851 --> 00:01:26.410
probably not the best idea. (laughing)

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:28.619
- It wasn't as bad as I
thought it was going to be.

00:01:28.619 --> 00:01:29.703
He was really chill.

00:01:29.703 --> 00:01:31.241
- Spencer here is a really good boy,

00:01:31.241 --> 00:01:33.718
and I'm very happy I
got to give you a bath,

00:01:33.718 --> 00:01:35.458
out of all the dogs in the world.

00:01:35.458 --> 00:01:37.231
- I actually really
connected with this dog.

00:01:37.231 --> 00:01:38.444
- I'm like smelling him now,

00:01:38.444 --> 00:01:40.761
and I feel like we didn't
do that good of a job,

00:01:40.761 --> 00:01:42.769
but that might just be the wet dog.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:43.659
- That's wet dog

00:01:43.659 --> 00:01:47.159
- I just don't really know dogs that well.

